# Captured fixtures are raw external-command output and must be preserved
# byte-for-byte — including CRLF line endings from Windows commands. Without
# this, core.autocrlf=true would rewrite them on commit and the parser tests
# would no longer be exercising real output. See skills/empirical-fixtures.
tests/fixtures/** -text

# ...but the capture script itself is a shell script that runs on Linux/macOS
# too — a CRLF shebang breaks it. Keep it LF regardless of the rule above and
# of core.autocrlf.
tests/fixtures/capture.sh text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
